detail.abstract:
This paper aims to bring the Fermi Paradox back into focus and use the Instability Model to resharpen and clearly define tools to make it more useful. The purpose is to assist with measuring probability of life using the Control: Feedback Ration and present a clear probability band.&nbsp;
<div>
 The tool proposed cannot predict life with certainty but allows for a comparative analysis between each other leading to probability. The scale of prediction works on individual planets, solar systems and even galactic scale.&nbsp;
</div>
<div>
 In previous works the Instability equation is clearly defined in this paper a Time variant (time) is introduced to track Instability over time leading to sharper more accurate predictions with a newly developed equation also introduced including a movement variant Omega-to account for direction of 3d systems.&nbsp;
</div>
<div>
 The scale of measurement already exists in form of the Kardashev Scale which is used to determine and attempt to solve the 'great filter Delima'&nbsp;
</div>
<div>
 The paper uses real existing mathematical physical equations and combines these with real world and difficult questions attempting to resolve the question is there a way to determine why we may be alone?
</div>
